.\" halite-sls(5)
.\"
.\" mdoc, like the section 8 pages. Every statement here is one the
.\" Handbook demonstrates against a running lab; chapters 5 and 6 carry
.\" the worked examples and the observed output.
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt HALITE-SLS 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SLS
.Nd the file format in which halite states are written
.Sh DESCRIPTION
An
.Nm
file is YAML describing the state a machine should be in.
A tree of them is applied by
.Xr halite-node 8
and served by
.Xr halite-hub 8 .
Applying a tree twice changes nothing the second time; this is what is meant
by idempotent, and every state function is expected to behave so.
.Pp
An SLS file is rendered as a template first (Jinja), then parsed as YAML.
.Sh DECLARATIONS
A declaration is a mapping from an
.Em ID
to a single
.Em module.function
whose value is a list of one-key mappings, the arguments:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
nginx_conf:
  file.managed:
    - name: /etc/nginx/nginx.conf
    - source: salt://webserver/files/nginx.conf
    - mode: '0644'
    - require:
      - pkg: nginx
.Ed
.Pp
The ID must be unique across the whole compiled tree, not only the file.
The argument
.Ar name
defaults to the ID.
A function with no arguments is written
.Ql pkg.installed: []
or bare as
.Ql pkg.installed .
.Pp
.Ar names
expands one declaration into one state per name; any other argument applies to
all of them.
.Sh YAML CAUTIONS
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Indent with spaces.
A tab is an error.
.It
A repeated key in one mapping is an error.
.It
.Ql mode: 0644
is the number 420 and is refused; write
.Ql mode: '0644' .
.It
.Ql yes ,
.Ql no ,
.Ql on
and
.Ql off
are booleans.
They are accepted, because existing trees depend on it, and each use is
reported as a warning with its file and line.
.El
.Sh REQUISITES
Order follows the order written unless a requisite says otherwise.
.Bl -tag -width "onchanges" -compact
.It Cm require
after the target, and only if it succeeded.
.It Cm watch
.Cm require ,
and also react if the target changed.
.It Cm onchanges
run only if the target reported changes.
.It Cm onfail
run only if the target failed.
.It Cm prereq
run before the target, and only if the target would change.
.It Cm use
inherit the target's arguments.
.It Cm listen
like
.Cm watch ,
but the reaction is deferred to the end of the run.
.El
.Pp
Each has an
.Ql _in
form written from the other side, and most an
.Ql _any
form satisfied by any one target.
A requisite names its target as
.Ql module: id .
.Sh TOP FILE
.Pa top.sls
maps environments and targets to the SLS files that apply to them.
The pillar has its own
.Pa top.sls .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr halite 7 ,
.Xr halite-node 8 ,
.Xr halite-hub 8
.Pp
The Handbook, chapters 4 to 7, in the
.Pa handbook/
directory of a release archive.
